e Landlord from discarding small cards.\n2. **Preserving Structure**: Using the 2 keeps my two Full Houses intact. If I were to use a J or 9, I would break these strong combinations.\n3. **Offensive Pressure**: Once I have the lead, I can play my Full Houses (999JJ, then 44433). The Landlord, missing many high cards (I hold 2, Teammate played 22), will struggle to beat these 5-card combinations. This strategy allows me to clear 11 of my 13 cards rapidly.\n4. **Teammate Support**: Since my teammate has few cards, taking the initiative relieves pressure from them and prevents the Landlord from dictating the flow with mid-range cards I cannot beat without breaking my hand.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♥2"]}'}
